Free installTrChar()'s translation buffer before rejecting an over-long
name, so the unserialize target stops leaking it.

installTrChar() (src/main/sysutils.c) translates the name into an
R_StringBuffer and passes it to install(), which raises "variable names
are limited to 10000 bytes" for an over-long result; that error unwinds
past the R_FreeStringBuffer() that follows.  Check the length first and
free the buffer before raising the same error.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 5066589054238720 (libFuzzer_r_unserialize,
Direct-leak; a symbol with an over-long translated name in the stream).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #370, filed 2026-10-10 (no Bugzilla
report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/sysutils.c
+++ b/src/main/sysutils.c
@@ -1891,6 +1891,11 @@
     // symbols with escapes, with a warning.
     translateToNative(CHAR(x), &cbuff, t, 2);
 
+    /* install() raises this itself, but then the buffer would leak. */
+    if (strlen(cbuff.data) > MAXIDSIZE) {
+	R_FreeStringBuffer(&cbuff);
+	error(_("variable names are limited to %d bytes"), MAXIDSIZE);
+    }
     SEXP Sans = install(cbuff.data);
     R_FreeStringBuffer(&cbuff);
     return Sans;
